# The shell scripts here run on Linux, in containers and on CI runners. A CRLF
# checkout on Windows turns `#!/usr/bin/env bash` into a file whose interpreter
# has a carriage return in its name, and the error says "no such file or
# directory" about a path that plainly exists.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
